# netsurf: borders paint at the composed group opacity (patch 314)
# Generated 2026-10-20
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 313)
#
# Doc 22 WS-A probe (a) / patch 311's recorded remainder: at partial
# group opacity, background fills (patch 149) and text (patch 311)
# faded, but borders painted solid -- an element at opacity .5 showed
# a full-strength frame around faded contents. Two breaks caused it:
# redraw_border.c set the border plot styles' opacity from the border
# colour's alpha byte only (patch 100), never the composed group
# opacity; and the vita plotter honoured a style's opacity bucket only
# on the geom fill path, so border trapezoids (polygon op), dashed and
# dotted borders (line op) and rectangle outlines drew solid even when
# the style carried alpha.
#
#  - redraw.c exports html_redraw_group_opacity(), the composed
#    g_group_opacity html_redraw_box maintains (the box's own opacity
#    multiplied by its ancestors', patch 149 composition, including
#    its dedup-by-shared-style semantics -- borders now match fills
#    and text exactly).
#  - html_redraw_border_plot folds that value into the border
#    colour's alpha before the plot styles are stamped, so every
#    border the core paints (block, inline, and fieldset borders all
#    pass through it; every border style) composes colour alpha x
#    group opacity. Folding ahead of the alpha == 0 early return also
#    drops an opacity: 0 subtree's borders entirely, as its fills and
#    text already vanish.
#  - the vita plotter takes the style's opacity bucket on the paths
#    borders travel: vita_plot_line_bucket() (the solid vita_plot_line
#    keeps its signature for chrome/replay callers), the polygon op's
#    fan fill and polyline stroke, and the rectangle op's outline
#    rects (its geom fill already bucketed). LINE and POLYGON traces
#    append " OPAQUE <bucket>" only when non-solid, so solid pages'
#    dumps stay byte-identical; replay.c honours the LINE suffix the
#    way patch 311 taught it for TEXT (POLYGON dumps are counts-only
#    there and tolerate the suffix).
#
# Side effect, intended: a translucent border COLOUR (patch 100, e.g.
# Tailwind's rgba(0,0,0,.1) dividers) previously blended only where
# the border happened to travel as a geom RECT fill; it now blends on
# the line and polygon paths too, as Firefox paints it.
#
# Proof (focused, sim): a 6px solid black border inside opacity:.5 --
# pre-fix RECT sides carry no token and snapshot pixels read 0,0,0;
# post-fix the sides carry OPAQUE 2 and read 127,127,127. Mixed-width
# borders (RECT decomposition) and dashed borders (LINE OPAQUE 2)
# read 127 on their strokes; a 9px double border paints 8 POLYGON
# OPAQUE 2 and reads 127 on its bands (controls token-free, solid).
# Composition: rgba(0,0,0,0.5) border standalone = OPAQUE 2 / pixel
# 127; the same border inside opacity:.5 = OPAQUE 1 / pixel 191 --
# colour alpha x group, exactly. Gate: CSS-opacity-group gains the
# four border boxes; the gate script asserts the counts above.
#
# Scope notes (recorded, not changed here):
#  - Images at partial opacity still paint opaque -- NOT bounded:
#    the bitmap plot op carries no opacity channel (its flags encode
#    blend mode only), the composed group opacity never reaches the
#    four image content handlers or the background-image call site
#    (they receive content + redraw_data, not the painting box), and
#    vita2d offers no tint-scale entry point in the stub/sim for a
#    texture drawn at alpha -- the device-side libvita2d entry cannot
#    be verified without vitaSDK. Closing images needs an op-channel
#    design first, like item 7 needed doc 19.
#  - The disc/arc ops and the SVG path filler likewise still draw at
#    VITA_BUCKET_SOLID regardless of the style's opacity (radio
#    buttons, list discs, SVG icons inside a group) -- same class,
#    recorded here rather than silently widening this patch.
#
# Simulator only; the vita cross-build was not run (no vitaSDK on
# this VM). Device expectation is in Doc 10.
